Based on the search results, the delimiter tactic used to wrap Java code when prompting an LLM to generate comments is **three hashes (`###`)**.

The prompt instructs the LLM to:
> "You are a Java Developer. Update the code delimited by three hashes and add in code comments to explain how the code works."

The Java code is then wrapped between opening and closing `###` delimiters:

```
###
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

public class Timesheet {
    // ... Java code here ...
}
###
```

This technique helps the LLM clearly identify where the code begins and ends, preventing it from mixing instructions with the code content and ensuring accurate comment generation without altering the original code structure.

